WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.438
Hi, I’m Sangmin, a moss farmer in Goyang, just northwest of Seoul.

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:07.798
I find possibilities in nature.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.950
I turn moss into products, from terrariums to commemorative plaques.

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:19.445
Making and selling them taught me to connect materials with real needs.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:26.471
With Urban Jungle, I design and build gardens and school forests.

00:00:26.471 --> 00:00:30.094
We make places where people can spend time with nature.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.186
Questions from the field also become software.

00:00:35.186 --> 00:00:41.468
Garden Atlas is a prototype for exploring landscape designs and sharing expert feedback.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.405
I make board games, tree cards, and published books.

00:00:48.405 --> 00:00:51.887
They give people a playful way to get closer to nature.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:59.208
I also plan and run cultural festivals.

00:00:59.208 --> 00:01:04.352
Gardens become places to meet, share stories, and learn from each other.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.661
What could we make together?

00:01:07.661 --> 00:01:14.581
Your local materials, knowledge, or community could meet my experience in one small experiment.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.333
Send me a photo or a question.

00:01:22.333 --> 00:01:26.410
Or visit Hacker Farm in Goyang, and let’s have a cup of tea.
